From 4ff9a952331780d73cd3f981a8cac02eef49a94c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:31:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 61/68] vgpu: mask unwritten fragment render-target locations
 and match color0 by slot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In Metal, omitting [[color(i)]] from a fragment shader's return type leaves attachment i untouched even when the render pipeline's color attachment descriptor carries the default MTLColorWriteMaskAll. Vulkan instead writes undefined values to any render-pass color attachment whose colorWriteMask is non-zero when the fragment output interface declares no Location = i (Vulkan 15.2).

Across macOS 27.2 RenderBox and WindowServer MRT passes, coverage-only shaders (Location 1), sublayer shaders (Locations 1 and 2), and color0-only shaders (Location 0) share multi-attachment render passes. Masking unwritten locations only when render_targets was completely empty — and before secondary_targets was populated — wiped sibling attachments (icon base plates, UI button labels, and Liquid Glass SDF/refraction maps) to zero.

Also resolve RenderPipelineDescriptor.color0 and the primary Vulkan attachment by slot == 0 rather than color_attachments.first(), preventing sparse secondary-only pipelines from aliasing slot 1's blend state onto slot 0.
